But if we special-case before recording, no count impact. Fine.

Let's apply. Also could use `method.getDeclaringClass() == Object.class` to ensure only Object methods. Use that condition.

```
if (method.getDeclaringClass() == Object.class) {
   switch(name) { case "hashCode": ...; case "equals": ...; case "toString": ...}
}
```
Default no such. This avoids overriding interface methods named equals (unlikely).

